                                <DTC ID="DTCB209845" OID="d0309d99-70a6-411e-9526-d61939a37083">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCB209845</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>10524741</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>B209845</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_692285185">Controller internal error</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_17015829">Service at next halt</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_790464762">1. Power reset</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1898635957">1. Power reset
2. UDS $85 ControlDTCSetting (Diag. On State)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1451217794">10ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_624397898">ECU RAM ECC failure</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_255659836">ECU RAM detection is successful in the next power-on cycle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1833380640">Record DTC; function degradation.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1932791118">1. Use service $14 to delete all DTC(s)
2. IGN 40 times ( have not current DTC)
* Refer to FM29_Spec-Book_CES_004_Basic_Diagnostics 4.3.3</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_119415551">1. Unexpeted RAM change error</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_21274392">Record DTC. Controller does not work properly</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCU13C088" OID="12b14030-ebf5-4f24-85de-2fc1571820e2">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCU13C088</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>13877384</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>U13C088</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1191749132">Detection CAN Busoff</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_17015829">Service at next halt</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_822339053">1. Check the Bus Line
2. Check the  HW</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1492207541">1. UDS $85 ControlDTCSetting ( Diag. On State)
2. No current DTC about voltage level (High and Low)
3. CAN Tx Enable state</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_1451217794">10ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_969703474">1. When TRANSCEIVER's Tx ERR COUNTER &gt; 255(several ms), the Bus Off statue occurs. (Bus off COUNTER = 0)
 - If Bus off flag is maintained after 950ms(tError), Bus off COUNTER + 1 = 1
(※Note: CAN Tx is prohibited when Bus off Counter is +1)
 - If Bus off flag is maintained after 950ms(tError), Bus off COUNTER + 1 = 2
 - DTC occurs when Bus off COUNTER = +2 is judged (Bus off DTC occurs after at least 1900ms after the first Bus off occurs)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1506380623">One of the messages was successfully transmitted. If it returns to normal, the fault can be restored to a historical fault during this power on cycle</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1833380640">Record DTC; function degradation.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_1932791118">1. Use service $14 to delete all DTC(s)
2. IGN 40 times ( have not current DTC)
* Refer to FM29_Spec-Book_CES_004_Basic_Diagnostics 4.3.3</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_1320332895">1. Circuit Short ,open</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_21274392">Record DTC. Controller does not work properly</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                            </DTCS>
                        </DTC-DOP>
